[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mThe translation verifies clean. The library turned out to be a single 37-line C translation unit with one public function, so I read it directly rather than delegating — a sub-agent round-trip would have cost more context than the source itself.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mWhat the C actually is:[22m [38;5;10mvoid driver(float x)[0m passes [38;5;10m&x[0m to a [38;5;10mstatic[0m helper [38;5;10mprint_hex[0m, which [38;5;10mprintf("%02x", p[i])[0ms the four bytes of the float's object representation in memory order, then [38;5;10mprintf("\n")[0m. No error channel, no options, no state.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mPhase A artifacts[22m ([38;5;10mtranslation/SYMBOLS.md[0m, [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m, [38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m), all derived by grepping the C rather than from assumptions:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- The C [38;5;10m.so[0m exports exactly one dynamic symbol, [38;5;10mdriver[0m. The Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m exports the same one; [38;5;10mnm -D[0m diff is empty. [38;5;10mprint_hex[0m is [38;5;10mstatic[0m and correctly exported by neither. Rust's undefined symbols are all libc/libgcc — notably both [38;5;10m.so[0ms import [38;5;10mputchar[0m, because the C compiler and LLVM independently applied the same [38;5;10mprintf("\n")[0m → [38;5;10mputchar('\n')[0m rewrite.[0m[0m
- ERRORS.md: [38;5;10mgrep[0m for [38;5;10mreturn[0m, [38;5;10massert[0m, [38;5;10mNULL[0m, [38;5;10merrno[0m, [38;5;10m-1[0m, [38;5;10mexit[0m, [38;5;10mabort[0m across all of [38;5;10mc_src/[0m returns [1mzero matches[22m; the only conditional in the whole library is the loop bound. The error surface is genuinely empty, so the 15 rows document the would-be rejection points the C deliberately does [3mnot[23m reject (NaN payloads, sNaN, −0.0, subnormals, FLT limits, the zero-pad and zero-extension paths) plus the required generic boundaries. There is no pointer parameter and no enum in the ABI, so those two boundaries are asserted structurally rather than invented.[0m[0m
- CONFIGS.md: 17 rows over the axes the C really branches on — per-byte value ([38;5;10m< 0x10[0m pad path, [38;5;10m>= 0x80[0m promotion path), IEEE-754 class and byte order, and call multiplicity on the shared [38;5;10mstdout[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mTesting:[22m [38;5;10mtests/[0m loads both [38;5;10m.so[0ms through [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and calls [38;5;10mdriver[0m only via [38;5;10mdlsym[0m — the Rust [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m wrapper is on the path of every assertion. Since [38;5;10mdriver[0m returns [38;5;10mvoid[0m, output is captured at the fd level ([38;5;10mdup[0m/[38;5;10mdup2[0m on fd 1 plus [38;5;10mfflush(NULL)[0m), which is the only way to observe what the C's [38;5;10mprintf[0m wrote. Each row compares the two captured streams byte-for-byte [3mand[23m against an independently computed [38;5;10mto_bits().to_le_bytes()[0m reference, so a row cannot pass by both sides being broken identically. Coverage includes a 65 536-input strided scan of the 32-bit space, exhaustive byte-value × byte-position coverage, and C/Rust interleaving in one capture window.[0m[0m
